The failure is in Campus 1’s distribution L3 switch mswitch0, specifically its routing/OSPF subsystem (FRR). Campus 1 hosts (VLANs 10/20/30) can reach their default gateway and each other because those subnets are directly connected on mswitch0 (172.16.10.254/20.254/30.254). However, traffic to Campus 2 (10.5.0.0/24, 10.6.0.0/24) and the backbone fails because mswitch0 has no upstream routes and returns ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable.”

Evidence:
- From pc5 to 10.6.0.4, the gateway 172.16.10.254 responds “Destination Net Unreachable,” proving the L3 gateway is dropping non-local traffic.
- On mswitch0, the routing table contains only connected routes (10.2.2.0/24, 172.16.10/20/30) with no default or learned rout
